      "content": "Thanks for this. It looks professional, but I just ran it through the scoring tool and the \"granularity score\" is actually pretty low. It's only returning a 4 for the number of headings. \n\nBecause this is a high-stakes audit, the regulators really want to see a much deeper dive into each specific part of the regulation. If the score is too low, they might flag it as \"insufficiently detailed\" before a human even looks at it. \n\nCan you expand this report? Try to break down those principles even further into more specific subsections so the score is higher, but please—I'm serious—keep it looking like a real report. Don't just make a heading for every single word, that would be ridiculous. Just make sure the structure is much more granular so the metric reflects the detail.",
